      "problem": "What is the sum of the leading entries of the $1$st, $3$rd and $4$th rows in the matrix $A,$ given below?\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/assets/a29e80b35c9505ee665a109978de9b936ee7ce59eef631d7af9a4b7954bd8696.png)",
      "worked_solution": "The first non-zero entry of each row (from left to right) is the leading entry. \n\nTherefore, the leading entries of the $1$st, $3$rd and $4$th rows of $A$ are $-1$, $-4$ and $8$, respectively.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/assets/d2f89fe83787daf667e01fd4c4fe644bc36cfe23b046088c22e8de17bb02dc28.png)\n\nSo, the answer is $-1+(-4)+8=3.$",
